---
/**
 * The session protocol reference, rendered from src/data/protocol.json — itself generated from the
 * product's docs/PROTOCOL.md and checked both ways against the wire's golden lines by CI
 * (scripts/gen-protocol.mjs, scripts/check-protocol.mjs).
 */
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import spec from '../../data/protocol.json';

const directions = [
	{ key: 'app_to_service', title: 'App → service', note: 'One JSON object per line on the child\'s stdin.' },
	{ key: 'service_to_app', title: 'Service → app', note: 'One JSON object per line on the child\'s stdout.' },
];
const enumLabels = {
	slot_kinds: 'Slot kinds',
	provider_failure_reasons: 'Provider failure reasons',
	turn_outcomes: 'Turn outcomes',
	confirmation_reasons: 'Confirmation reasons',
};
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Session protocol reference',
		description:
			'Every message in the app↔service protocol v1: JSON lines over the child\'s stdin and stdout, with each message\'s fields and meaning — generated from PROTOCOL.md and checked against the golden lines.',
	}}
	headings={[
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'framing', text: 'Framing' },
		...directions.map((d) => ({ depth: 2, slug: d.key.replaceAll('_', '-'), text: d.title })),
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'identifiers', text: 'Identifiers' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'enumerations', text: 'Enumerations' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'ordering', text: 'Ordering guarantees' },
	]}
>
	<p>
		This is Personal Voice Agent's only "API": the line protocol between the app and the
		<code>voice-session</code> child it launches. It is generated from the product's
		<code>docs/PROTOCOL.md</code> and verified both ways against the golden lines the Rust and
		Swift suites decode — a message or field that exists only here, or only on the wire, fails CI.
		The raw document is at <a href="/protocol.json"><code>/protocol.json</code></a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="framing">Framing</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>One JSON object per line, UTF-8, terminated by <code>\n</code>, carrying a <code>"type"</code>.</li>
		<li>A line over {spec.framing.max_line_bytes.toLocaleString()} bytes is rejected (<code>error</code> <code>line_too_long</code>) and discarded to its newline.</li>
		<li>An unknown <code>type</code> or malformed JSON is <code>error</code> <code>bad_message</code>; the session continues.</li>
		<li>The first app message must be <code>{spec.framing.first_message}</code>; anything else first is <code>error</code> <code>hello_required</code>.</li>
		<li>stdin EOF ends the session cleanly.</li>
		<li>Audio never crosses this boundary: it stays in the app and is never written to disk.</li>
	</ul>

	{
		directions.map(({ key, title, note }) => (
			<>
				<h2 id={key.replaceAll('_', '-')}>{title}</h2>
				<p>{note}</p>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th><code>type</code></th>
							<th>Fields</th>
							<th>Meaning</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{Object.entries(spec[key]).map(([type, message]) => (
							<tr>
								<td><code>{type}</code></td>
								<td>{message.fields.length === 0 ? '—' : message.fields.map((f) => <code>{f}</code>).reduce((a, b) => <>{a}, {b}</>)}</td>
								<td>{message.meaning}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</>
		))
	}

	<h2 id="identifiers">Identifiers</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>turn</code> — u64, increasing within a session; <code>0</code> is never used.</li>
		<li><code>call</code> — u64, increasing within a session; one per provider request, capture window or tool call.</li>
		<li><code>digest</code> — 16 hex digits binding a confirmation to one proposal of one turn. A binding identifier, not a cryptographic hash.</li>
		<li><code>session</code> — the service's run id (a UUID), reported once in <code>ready</code>.</li>
		<li><code>seq</code> — a chunk's order inside its turn (<code>tts_request</code>), or a liveness/flush counter (<code>ping</code>→<code>pong</code>, <code>flush</code>→<code>flushed</code>).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="enumerations">Enumerations</h2>
	<dl>
		{Object.entries(spec.enums).map(([key, list]) => (
			<>
				<dt>{enumLabels[key] ?? key}</dt>
				<dd>{list.map((v) => <code>{v}</code>).reduce((a, b) => <>{a}, {b}</>)}</dd>
			</>
		))}
	</dl>
	<p>
		The <code>proposal</code> an <code>lm_done</code> carries is <code>{`{"kind":"reply","reply":"…"}`}</code> or
		<code>{`{"kind":"action","reply":"…","tool":"…","slots":[{"name":"…","kind":"…","value":"…"}]}`}</code>.
		An action's <code>reply</code> is never spoken. There is no external-effect confirmation reason: an external
		tool is refused before any confirmation, because no external action can be authorized in the first release.
	</p>

	<h2 id="ordering">Ordering guarantees</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>For a turn, the service sends <code>capture on</code> only after <code>turn_opened</code>, and every provider request for turn N before <code>turn_closed</code> for N.</li>
		<li><code>stop_playback</code> for an interrupted turn is sent before the <code>turn_closed</code> that records the interruption, and before <code>turn_opened</code> of a following turn.</li>
		<li>After <code>cancel</code>, replies for that <code>call</code> are dropped (and recorded as dropped); they never change the turn.</li>
	</ul>
</StarlightPage>
